<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins Japan order worth 500 mln skr.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins Japan order worth 500 mln skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecommunications company L.M. Ericsson AB said it won an order from Japan's Digital Tuka Kyushu (DTQ) worth 500 million crowns to develop its mobile telephony system.  </p>
<p>The order for AXE switchgear and radio base stations is for both users and operators and will be ready for use in 1997.</p>
<p>Six mobile operators in Japan have chosen Ericsson as systems supplier.</p>
<p>Ericsson said Japan has at present 16 million mobile phone subscribers, and that the figure will rise to 53 million by the millennium.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
